  version = "0.15.0",
  items = {
    { "Clearer names", "the narrators now say Goretusk, Runetotem, Soulscar and seven other two-word names clearly.", "Clearer names:" },
    { "Your place and quests in your language", "reading in another language on an English game client, the panel's header, its Here line and your quest list show the zone, subzone and quest names a client in that language uses, not English. A name we don't have yet stays as your game shows it.", "Your place and quests in your language:" },
    { "Your profile tells your journey", "it opens with your story, then your journey in chapters, one for each day you played: where you went, the dungeons and bosses, levels, new lands and the pictures you took there, with every moment folded inside. On a wide screen the map stays beside you and follows the chapter you're reading, and your numbers have a tab of their own.", "Your profile tells your journey:" },
    { "Ask about the creature you're fighting", "with a wolf, boar, bat or other wild animal targeted, \"why are they attacking me?\" now answers about that creature, like where Northshire's wolves came from, instead of about bandits or other trouble nearby.", "Ask about the creature you're fighting:" },
    { "Setup no longer looks stuck at the end of a download", "while extra narration downloads, Setup counts the megabytes, and once the last byte is in, a moving bar says it's checking and unpacking the files, which can take a few minutes for quest narration.", "Setup no longer looks stuck at the end of a download:" },
    { "Class lore matches WoW Forever", "the class and race entries now say who can walk which path in Forever, from Forsaken paladins and dwarf shaman to gnome priests, human hunters, orc mages, troll warlocks and the Skyborne.", "Class lore matches WoW Forever:" },
    { "Mount Hyjal and a WoW Forever overview", "new entries for the night elves' sacred mountain and for Forever's world, its lands, dungeons and raids, so the add-on and the companion can answer \"what's in WoW Forever?\"", "Mount Hyjal and a WoW Forever overview:" },
    { "More answers read aloud", "the male narrator now reads 7,570 more answers about places, lore, people and quests (11,160 in all), and the female narrator 5,844 more, including her first answers about quests in the third part and 2,864 more about lore items.", "More answers read aloud:" },
    { "Willo never leaves you at a dead end", "when today's live answers are used up, Willo answers from the add-on's lore library instead, and says when live answers come back.", "Willo never leaves you at a dead end:" },
    { "French and Spanish narration on CurseForge", "Lore Forever's CurseForge file now lists the French and Spanish narration for both narrators as optional downloads, next to German and Portuguese, along with German quest dialogue, the quest givers' voices, the female narrator's answers and the Russian and Ukrainian packs.", "French and Spanish narration on CurseForge:" },
    { "Narration in your language, and how to hear it", "with German, French, Spanish or Portuguese narration installed while Lore Forever shows English (Automatic on an English game client), login now says once which narration that is and how to switch to it, instead of quietly playing the English voices.", "Narration in your language, and how to hear it:" },
    { "Battlegrounds have their story", "Warsong Gulch, Arathi Basin, Alterac Valley and Forever's own Darkspear Islands now have lore entries on who fights there and what each side is fighting for, shown when you enter one.", "Battlegrounds have their story:" },
    { "Battles are told as battles", "your journey now records each battleground you fight in: which one, your side, who won, and your own honorable kills, killing blows, deaths and objectives. Ask Willo \"What am I doing?\" after one and it tells it as a battle, with what was at stake and how you did, not as a string of deaths with companions. The journey page and your profile story say so too.", "Battles are told as battles:" },
    { "Share anonymous usage counts", "the companion's daily check-in now also tells us how often each feature of the add-on and Willo gets used, so we can build more of what players love. Only numbers and a few choices (voice, language, level range, settings), never what you ask, hear or write, and no account needed. The companion's setting, now called Share anonymous usage counts, turns it off.", "Share anonymous usage counts:" },
    { "Hear what each download adds before you get it", "the Downloads page opens with one download button and what comes with it, then a tile for each extra pack (the female narrator, recorded answers, quest dialogue and the quest givers' voices) with lines you can play, its count and size. \"Your language\" gathers the text, narrators and quest dialogue for each language in one place. Every lore page now says which downloads have its recording.", "Hear what each download adds before you get it:" },
    { "Lua errors are easy to report", "when Lore Forever hits a Lua error, the chat says so once, and /lore errors shows what happened (the error, where, how often and the version) in a box to copy into the feedback page or Discord. Nothing is sent by itself, and other add-ons and the game's own error window still see every error.", "Lua errors are easy to report:" },
    { "German and French narration, now with native voices", "the German and French narrators read most zone, place, dungeon and boss stories again, in a native accent and from today's translations: German 644 stories (male) and 498 (female), French 533 and 532, up from 52 to 72 each. Stories not yet re-recorded stay available as text.", "German and French narration, now with native voices:" },
    { "More complete stories", "195 more zones, subzones and characters play their whole story: 110 in the male narrator's voice and 85 in the female narrator's. 23 stories that lore fixes had changed play in full again.", "More complete stories:" },
